# 002-room-folders.lua

The front door of room-folders: opens a rao-home, reads and writes its
settings and contacts, makes, reads and changes rooms, and rings the change
bell after every room change.  Load with `require("002-room-folders")` after
`001-load-path.lua` has been run.

A **home** is a table `{ dir = string }` (absolute path of rao-home).
A **room id** is a string of 32 lower-case hexadecimal characters.
"No parent" is the empty string `""`.

## Home and settings

| function | takes | gives | what it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `open_home(dir)` | dir: string, absolute | home | Makes `dir`, `config`, `contacts`, `rooms/`, `people/` if missing; leaves existing ones alone.  Errors on a relative path, a missing folder above `dir`, or `dir` being a file. |
| `read_config(home)` | home | table string→string | Every setting in `config`.  Values stay strings (`"true"` is not a boolean).  Errors on a malformed line or a key set twice. |
| `set_config(home, key, value)` | home, key: string (`[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+`), value: string (one line, no edge spaces) | nothing | Rewrites the key's line in place (comments and order kept) or appends it. |
| `config_value(home, key)` | home, key: string | string | The value; **errors** when the key is absent, naming the line to add.  Every undecided choice is read through this. |
| `read_contacts(home)` | home | table name (string) → table field (string) → value (string) | rmail's contacts format.  Indexed fields keep their index in the field name (`c["ip[2]"]`); double quotes are stripped; repeated plain `ip` lines are numbered as rmail does. |

## Rooms

| function | takes | gives | what it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| `new_room_id()` | — | room id | 16 bytes of `/dev/urandom` as hex. |
| `is_room_id(value)` | anything | bool | Whether `value` is a well-formed room id. |
| `create_room(home, spec)` | spec: `{ name = string, parent_id = string, recipients = list of string, room_id = room id or nil }` | room id | Builds the room (`name`, `parent`, `recipients`, empty `log`) in a hidden folder and renames it into place, then rings `"created"`.  Refuses: bad or used id, empty or multi-line name, a loop, bad recipient names, repeats, `"me"`. |
| `read_room(home, id)` | home, room id | `{ id = string, name = string, parent_id = string, recipients = list of string }` | Reads the three files fresh.  Errors on a missing room or a damaged file. |
| `write_name(home, id, name)` | home, room id, string | nothing | Rewrites `name`, rings `"name"`. |
| `write_parent(home, id, parent_id)` | home, room id, string (`""` or room id) | nothing | Rewrites `parent`, rings `"parent"`.  Refuses a loop. |
| `write_recipients(home, id, list)` | home, room id, list of string | nothing | Rewrites `recipients`, rings `"recipients"`.  An empty list is an empty file. |
| `list_rooms(home)` | home | sorted list of room ids | Skips hidden (half-built) entries; errors on any other stranger in `rooms/`. |
| `room_exists(home, id)` | home, room id | bool | Whether the room's folder exists. |
| `room_dir(home, id)` | home, room id | string | `<home>/rooms/<id>`; errors on a malformed id. |
| `log_path(home, id)` | home, room id | string | `<home>/rooms/<id>/log`. |

## The change bell (from 005-change-bell)

| function | takes | gives |
|---|---|---|
| `on_change(listener)` | function(home, room_id, what) | nothing |
| `notify(home, id, what)` | home, string, one of `created name parent recipients log removed-room split` | nothing; a listener's error passes through |
| `listener_count()` | — | integer |

## Settings read only on an edge case

| key | read when | values |
|---|---|---|
| `rooms.unknown-parent` | a parent id names a room with no folder here | `refuse`, `keep` |
| `rooms.slash-in-name` | a room name contains `/` | `refuse`, `allow` |
